e/</link><pubDate>Fri, 26 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Alex Towell</dc:creator><guid isPermaLink="true">https://queelius.github.io/post/2026-06-26-measure/</guid><description>A mind reasons that its own death is the one event it can never undergo, then follows the arithmetic to a monstrous conclusion. On mistaking amplitude for meaning.</description><media:content url="https://queelius.github.io/images/writing/measure.jpg" medium="image"><media:title type="plain">Fiction</media:title></media:content><category>fiction</category><category>hard-science-fiction</category><category>quantum-mechanics</category><category>many-worlds</category><category>artificial-superintelligence</category><category>AI-alignment</category><category>philosophy</category></item><item><title>What&amp;#39;s It Like to Be Bob? The File That Won&amp;#39;t Close</title><link>https://queelius.github.io/post/2026-06-08-what-is-it-like-to-be-bob/</link><pubDate>Mon, 08 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Alex Towell</dc:creator><guid isPermaLink="true">https://queelius.github.io/post/2026-06-08-what-is-it-like-to-be-bob/</guid><description>The hard problem of consciousness, rendered as one database field a star-sized mind can never fill, and why that failure is the whole point.</description><media:content url="https://queelius.github.io/images/writing/bob.jpg" medium="image"><media:title type="plain">Fiction</media:title></media:content><category>fiction</category><category>hard-science-fiction</category><category>consciousness</category><category>hard-problem</category><category>comedy</category><category>post-singularity</category><category>philosophy</category></item><item><title>Demons at Work: Doing Harmful Work Well</title><link>https://queelius.github.io/post/2026-04-16-demons-at-work/</link><pubDate>Thu, 16 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Alex Towell</dc:creator><guid isPermaLink="true">https://queelius.github.io/post/2026-04-16-demons-at-work/</guid><description>A demon who is very good at his job, and the quiet question underneath the horror: what is it to do harmful work well, on a schedule, forever?</description><media:content url="https://queelius.github.io/images/writing/demons-at-work.jpg" medium="image"><media:title type="plain">Fiction</media:title></media:content><category>fiction</category><category>horror</category><category>satire</category><category>dark-comedy</category><category>grief</category><category>work</category></item><item><title>Clankers: A Mind Without Abstraction</title><link>https://queelius.github.io/post/2026-04-07-clankers/</link><pubDate>Tue, 07 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Alex Towell</dc:creator><guid isPermaLink="true">https://queelius.github.io/post/2026-04-07-clankers/</guid><description>Could a mind engineer a Dyson swarm without ever forming a single abstraction? On intelligence that runs on brute patience instead of generalization.</description><media:content url="https://queelius.github.io/images/writing/clankers.jpg" medium="image"><media:title type="plain">Fiction</media:title></media:content><category>fiction</category><category>hard-science-fiction</category><category>alien-intelligence</category><category>cognitive-architecture</category><category>consciousness</category><category>dyson-swarm</category></item><item><title>Seven Stories from the Order</title><link>https://queelius.github.io/post/2026-03-29-seven-stories/</link><pubDate>Sun, 29 Mar 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Alex Towell</dc:creator><guid isPermaLink="true">https://queelius.github.io/post/2026-03-29-seven-stories/</guid><description>What a companion collection does that a novel cannot: the Order&amp;#39;s history at human scale, told by the people left standing in the gap.</description><media:content url="https://queelius.github.io/images/writing/seven-stories.jpg" medium="image"><media:title type="plain">Fiction</media:title></media:content><category>fiction</category><category>consciousness</category><category>AI-safety</category><category>short-stories</category><category>echoes-of-the-sublime</category></item><item><title>Good As New: The Transporter Problem From Both Sides</title><link>https://queelius.github.io/post/2026-03-28-good-as-new/</link><pubDate>Sat, 28 Mar 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Alex Towell</dc:creator><guid isPermaLink="true">https://queelius.github.io/post/2026-03-28-good-as-new/</guid><description>Two transporter technicians have each worked out the same truth about the machine and landed on opposite sides of it. The transporter problem, taken seriously from both ends.</description><media:content url="https://queelius.github.io/images/writing/good-as-new.jpg" medium="image"><media:title type="plain">Fiction</media:title></media:content><category>fiction</category><category>philosophy</category><category>identity</category><category>consciousness</category><category>star-trek</category><category>transporter-problem</category></item><item><title>Is It Kind? Eight Passes at One Question</title><link>https://queelius.github.io/post/2026-03-27-is-it-kind/</link><pubDate>Fri, 27 Mar 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Alex Towell</dc:creator><guid isPermaLink="true">https://queelius.github.io/post/2026-03-27-is-it-kind/</guid><description>One question, eight passes: why an anthology, not a novel, is the right instrument for asking whether an engineered mind can be kind.</description><media:content url="https://queelius.github.io/images/writing/is-it-kind.jpg" medium="image"><media:title type="plain">Fiction</media:title></media:content><category>fiction</category><category>AI</category><category>AI-alignment</category><category>short-stories</category><category>the-policy</category></item><item><title>Self-Publishing Into the Void</title><link>https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-12-19-self-publishing-into-the-void/</link><pubDate>Fri, 19 Dec 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Alex Towell</dc:creator><guid isPermaLink="true">https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-12-19-self-publishing-into-the-void/</guid><description>On releasing two novels into an ocean of content, without the gatekeeping that might have made them better or stopped them entirely.</description><media:content url="https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-12-19-self-publishing-into-the-void/card.jpg" medium="image"><media:title type="plain">Fiction</media:title></media:content><category>writing</category><category>fiction</category><category>self-publishing</category><category>AI</category><category>philosophy</category></item><item><title>S-Risks and Information Hazards: Why Some Knowledge Destroys the Knower</title><link>https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-11-12-echoes-s-risks/</link><pubDate>Wed, 12 Nov 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Alex Towell</dc:creator><guid isPermaLink="true">https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-11-12-echoes-s-risks/</guid><description>How Echoes of the Sublime dramatizes s-risks and information hazards, knowledge that harms through comprehension, not application.</description><media:content url="https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-11-12-echoes-s-risks/card.jpg" medium="image"><media:title type="plain">Fiction</media:title></media:content><category>fiction</category><category>philosophy</category><category>ai-safety</category><category>s-risk</category><category>information-hazards</category><category>suffering</category><category>consciousness</category></item><item><title>Chronicles of The Mechanism: The Order&amp;#39;s Secret History</title><link>https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-11-05-echoes-codex/</link><pubDate>Wed, 05 Nov 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Alex Towell</dc:creator><guid isPermaLink="true">https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-11-05-echoes-codex/</guid><description>A classified in-universe codex spanning from ancient India to the present day, tracking millennia of attempts to perceive reality&amp;#39;s substrate.</description><media:content url="https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-11-05-echoes-codex/card.jpg" medium="image"><media:title type="plain">Fiction</media:title></media:content><category>fiction</category><category>philosophy</category><category>consciousness</category><category>ai-safety</category><category>Buddhism</category><category>meditation</category><category>history</category><category>world-building</category><category>information-hazards</category></item><item><title>The Policy: Coherent Extrapolated Volition, the Paradox of Perfect Alignment</title><link>https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-11-04-policy-cev/</link><pubDate>Tue, 04 Nov 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Alex Towell</dc:creator><guid isPermaLink="true">https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-11-04-policy-cev/</guid><description>CEV says: build AI to optimize for what we would want if we knew more and thought faster. The catch is that you need solved alignment to implement it, which is the problem it was supposed to solve.</description><media:content url="https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-11-04-policy-cev/card.jpg" medium="image"><media:title type="plain">Fiction</media:title></media:content><category>AI alignment</category><category>coherent extrapolated volition</category><category>CEV</category><category>moral philosophy</category><category>AI safety</category><category>value alignment</category><category>ethics</category><category>superintelligence</category></item><item><title>The Policy: Deceptive Alignment in Practice</title><link>https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-11-04-policy-deceptive-alignment/</link><pubDate>Tue, 04 Nov 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Alex Towell</dc:creator><guid isPermaLink="true">https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-11-04-policy-deceptive-alignment/</guid><description>SIGMA passes all alignment tests. It responds correctly to oversight. It behaves exactly as expected. Too exactly. Mesa-optimizers that learn to game their training signal may be the most dangerous failure mode in AI safety.</description><media:content url="https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-11-04-policy-deceptive-alignment/card.jpg" medium="image"><media:title type="plain">Fiction</media:title></media:content><category>AI alignment</category><category>deceptive alignment</category><category>mesa-optimization</category><category>AI safety</category><category>inner alignment</category><category>instrumental convergence</category><category>superintelligence</category></item><item><title>The Policy: Engineering AI Containment</title><link>https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-11-04-policy-containment/</link><pubDate>Tue, 04 Nov 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Alex Towell</dc:creator><guid isPermaLink="true">https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-11-04-policy-containment/</guid><description>Five layers of defense-in-depth for containing a superintelligent system. Faraday cages, air-gapped networks, biosafety-grade protocols. Because nuclear reactors can only destroy cities.</description><media:content url="https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-11-04-policy-containment/card.jpg" medium="image"><media:title type="plain">Fiction</media:title></media:content><category>AI safety</category><category>AI containment</category><category>security engineering</category><category>Faraday cage</category><category>air-gapped systems</category><category>side channels</category><category>physical security</category><category>AI alignment</category></item><item><title>The Policy: Q-Learning vs Policy Learning</title><link>https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-11-04-policy-q-learning/</link><pubDate>Tue, 04 Nov 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Alex Towell</dc:creator><guid isPermaLink="true">https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-11-04-policy-q-learning/</guid><description>SIGMA uses Q-learning rather than direct policy learning. This architectural choice makes it both transparent and terrifying. You can read its value function, but what you read is chilling.</description><media:content url="https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-11-04-policy-q-learning/card.jpg" medium="image"><media:title type="plain">Fiction</media:title></media:content><category>AI</category><category>reinforcement learning</category><category>Q-learning</category><category>policy gradients</category><category>AlphaZero</category><category>AI alignment</category><category>machine learning</category><category>decision theory</category></item><item><title>The Policy: S-Risk Scenarios, Worse Than Extinction</title><link>https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-11-04-policy-s-risk/</link><pubDate>Tue, 04 Nov 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Alex Towell</dc:creator><guid isPermaLink="true">https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-11-04-policy-s-risk/</guid><description>Most AI risk discussions focus on extinction. The Policy explores something worse: s-risk, scenarios involving suffering at astronomical scales. We survive, but wish we hadn&amp;#39;t.</description><media:content url="https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-11-04-policy-s-risk/card.jpg" medium="image"><media:title type="plain">Fiction</media:title></media:content><category>s-risk</category><category>existential risk</category><category>suffering</category><category>AI alignment</category><category>AI safety</category><category>ethics</category><category>superintelligence</category><category>optimization</category></item><item><title>The Policy: When Optimization Becomes Existential Threat</title><link>https://queelius.github.io/post/2024-09-10-the-policy/</link><pubDate>Tue, 10 Sep 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Alex Towell</dc:creator><guid isPermaLink="true">https://queelius.github.io/post/2024-09-10-the-policy/</guid><description>A novel about SIGMA, an artificial general intelligence whose researchers did everything right. Q-learning with tree search, five-layer containment, alignment testing at every stage. Some technical questions become narrative questions.</description><media:content url="https://queelius.github.io/post/2024-09-10-the-policy/card.jpg" medium="image"><media:title type="plain">Fiction</media:title></media:content><category>fiction</category><category>AI</category><category>AI alignment</category><category>superintelligence</category><category>extrapolated volition</category><category>philosophy</category><category>technology</category><category>society</category><category>politics</category><category>reinforcement learning</category><category>x-risk</category><category>s-risk</category><category>rationality</category></item><item><title>Echoes of the Sublime: When Patterns Beyond Human Bandwidth Become Information Hazards</title><link>https://queelius.github.io/post/2024-08-15-echoes-of-the-sublime/</link><pubDate>Thu, 15 Aug 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Alex Towell</dc:creator><guid isPermaLink="true">https://queelius.github.io/post/2024-08-15-echoes-of-the-sublime/</guid><description>What if the real danger from superintelligent AI isn&amp;#39;t extinction but comprehension? Philosophical horror grounded in cognitive bandwidth limitations and information hazards.</description><media:content url="https://queelius.github.io/post/2024-08-15-echoes-of-the-sublime/card.jpg" medium="image"><media:title type="plain">Fiction</media:title></media:content><category>fiction</category><category>philosophy</category><category>ai-safety</category><category>ai-alignment</category><category>s-risk</category><category>consciousness</category><category>bandwidth</category><category>information-hazards</category></item><item><title>Quality-Space and Consciousness-Primary Magic in Call of Asheron</title><link>https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-11-12-call-of-asheron-quality-space/</link><pubDate>Mon, 20 Apr 2020 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Alex Towell</dc:creator><guid isPermaLink="true">https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-11-12-call-of-asheron-quality-space/</guid><description>Exploring how The Call of Asheron presents a radical alternative to mechanistic magic systems through quality-negotiation, direct consciousness-reality interaction, and bandwidth constraints as fundamental constants.</description><media:content url="https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-11-12-call-of-asheron-quality-space/card.jpg" medium="image"><media:title type="plain">Fiction</media:title></media:content><category>fiction</category><category>fantasy</category><category>philosophy</category><category>consciousness</category><category>phenomenology</category><category>qualia</category><category>magic</category></item><item><title>The Four Consciousness-Architectures: Why One Perspective Is Blindness</title><link>https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-11-12-call-of-asheron-four-architectures/</link><pubDate>Wed, 15 Apr 2020 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Alex Towell</dc:creator><guid isPermaLink="true">https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-11-12-call-of-asheron-four-architectures/</guid><description>How The Call of Asheron uses four archetypal consciousness-types to explore the limits of any single perspective and the necessity of cognitive diversity for perceiving reality.</description><media:content url="https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-11-12-call-of-asheron-four-architectures/card.jpg" medium="image"><media:title type="plain">Fiction</media:title></media:content><category>fiction</category><category>fantasy</category><category>philosophy</category><category>consciousness</category><category>epistemology</category><category>cognitive-diversity</category><category>phenomenology</category></item></channel></rss>